**Empathy Map Key Findings

* Users need a clear explanation of what they will gain from the Movement to Work programme
* Users may be unsure where to begin when searching for work experience or employment
* Large amounts of content can make it difficult for users to find the information they need
* Users may lack confidence in using AI for job applications and need clear guidance on appropriate use
* Users want practical support with CVs, job applications and interview preparation
* Users need reassurance that the programme will genuinely help them gain useful work experience
* Clear next steps are important so users always understand what to do next
* Trust is important, particularly when users are relying on employment advice and programme information
* Users need help understanding how to tailor their CV towards specific job roles
* The skills gained from the programme should be clearly explained before users decide to take part
* Users are likely to scan headings, imagery and short sections rather than read large blocks of text
* Information should come from sources users recognise as trustworthy
* Interactive content may help users understand their options and remain engaged
* Users may seek additional guidance when they are unsure about job preparation
* Users can feel overwhelmed when too much information is presented at once
* Users may be interested in how AI can support employment but still need reassurance and education around its use
* Privacy and the handling of personal information can be a concern
* Users may feel uncertain about how to sign up for Movement to Work
* Difficulty finding relevant information can lead to frustration
* Users may not know which job roles or employment sectors are suitable for them
* The overall experience should provide a simple journey from understanding the programme to preparing for employment
